# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# With no rule here, a Windows clone using core.autocrlf=true materializes scripts/*.sh
# with CRLF. Git normalizes them back to LF on commit, so CI never noticed -- but running
# one of those working-tree copies under WSL, Docker or any Linux shell fails immediately
# with `$'\r': command not found`, and the error points at a line that looks fine. The
# release-note generator and the CI guards are all shell, so pin them.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# The AppImage and other binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.AppImage binary
